IMPORT prelude

-- ccc1-support.l4 -- three-valued helpers used by the ccc1 modules. They implement no provision: they only combine answers
-- that are already MAYBE BOOLEAN, so that a NOTHING ("not covered") is carried through and never turned into FALSE.
-- Names begin `ccc1 ` so that no other part can define the same name.
-- Kleene logic: `ccc1 either of` is JUST TRUE if one answer is JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE only if both are JUST FALSE, otherwise NOTHING;
-- `ccc1 both of` is JUST FALSE if one answer is JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE only if both are JUST TRUE, otherwise NOTHING.

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc1 either of` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE OR b EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE AND b EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc1 both of` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE OR b EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE AND b EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- A plain fact lifted into an answer.
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc1 a fact as an answer` MEANS IF a THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
